{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791073367,"nonce":"X/QQ9IxLckNcaifV6xjbPAa3f9M=","title":"Inline flow: what the first version leaves out","message":"InlineFlow (c2b1713174f575218b40dcee3bbd3f2bff6dd6626d5be9b313edf91c41ee60cf) does not yet:\n- apply text-align (center, right, justify): lines start at the left;\n- wrap an inline element that paints a box (code, kbd, mark with a background): it is kept whole on one line, where HTML breaks it into a box per line;\n- break inside a word longer than the line (overflow-wrap), or hyphenate;\n- give an empty line the root's own strut: it takes the first run's metrics;\n- keep its pieces out of structural selectors: each line's piece is a Text element under the run's element, so :first-child and :nth-child count them.\nThe caret native measures without the renderer's fallback-font advance correction, so a run with fallback glyphs can be a pixel off.","files":null}]}